WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.700
Next, a real life love story

2
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.197
that shows timing is everything.

3
00:00:03.197 --> 00:00:06.240
"People" reports, a couple named Paul Mattingly

4
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.680
and Laura Lee Estees got married

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.790
for the second time over the pandemic

6
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.150
after living apart for 40 years.

7
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.570
Oh, look at 'em.
Their first wedding

8
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.690
was in 1980, fresh outta college.

9
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.030
They were too young to make it work.

10
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.140 line:15%
And then, they divorced and they drifted apart.

11
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.530 line:15%
But then in 2019, Laura Lee was passing through Paul's town

12
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.363 line:15%
and reached out.

13
00:00:25.363 --> 00:00:27.880 line:15%
"And did he wanna go to dinner?", she asked.

14
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.850 line:15%
They were both single.

15
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.390 line:15%
Paul says the moment he saw her,

16
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.010 line:15%
it was love at second sight.
Oh.

17
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.247 line:15%
Laura Lee said, "It was like seeing the best friend

18
00:00:35.247 --> 00:00:36.410 line:15%
"you haven't seen in years."

19
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.550 line:15%
And they just celebrated their one year anniversary

20
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.383 line:15%
in their 60's.

21
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:42.189 line:15%
And now, their mantra is they just wanna make up

22
00:00:42.189 --> 00:00:43.850 line:15%
for lost time.

23
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.120 line:15%
I love this.
This is so cute.

24
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.760 line:15%
That goes into timing is everything too.

25
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.790 line:15%
Absolutely, and what I call this,

26
00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.623
I've said here before,

27
00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:53.640
I love when people hook up again.

28
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.820
I call it reheating your leftovers

29
00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.330
when it's been in the fridge for a while.

30
00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.630
You liked it once, maybe I just nuke it a little bit,

31
00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:00.500
I'll want it again.

32
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.270
40 years, I hope it was in the freezer

33
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.170
and not the fridge.
Yeah, in a nice Tupperware.

34
00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.633
Yeah, a little like Walt Disney cryo Stitch.

35
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.350
Are there any leftovers in your fridge

36
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.250
that you just can't stop thinking about,

37
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.670
maybe one day you're just gonna heat 'em up?

38
00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.700
Are we talking about boys or soups?

39
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.880
I was not talking about soup.

40
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.140
Yes, I have revisited a few exes

41
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.750
and I keep coming up with the same thing,

42
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.960
which is a lot of good self discovery

43
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.730
that I've really grown up a lot

44
00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.110
and I've made a lot of concerted effort

45
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.380
to kind of change my patterns and behaviors,

46
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.370
so it's kind of like all good news.

47
00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.203
It is good news.

48
00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:39.560
And I do believe timing is everything.

49
00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.070
You could meet the right person at the wrong time.

50
00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:42.903
And clearly they didn't.

51
00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:45.930
How beautiful they reconnected 40 years later

52
00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:46.910
for their love story.
I think it's very helpful.

53
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:47.743
I love it too.

54
00:01:47.743 --> 00:01:49.030
I love it.
I love it.

55
00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.610
Yeah, none of my exes are interested

56
00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.960
and there's nothing there.

57
00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.980
They're all bird carcasses.

58
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.680
Oh my God!
(all laugh)

59
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.350
I'm telling you, all the relationships

60
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.940
in my past are like, there's nothing left,

61
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.000
there's nothing to revisit.

62
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.800
You've picked all of the meat off.

63
00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.747
It's like vultures flying over and they're like,

64
00:02:10.747 --> 00:02:13.759
"Nothing to eat here, move it along, boys!"

65
00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:16.342 line:15%
(upbeat music)

